==Strategy==
This stage can be particularly difficult (relative to the stages leading up to it), given that the restriction disables many [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]] like [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] and [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]], and there is a rush of Starred Aliens that can easily push back the player's cats.

==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
The strategies in the Walkthroughs should be doable with just Normal/Special Cats, and only the [[Treasure]]s from before this level.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage can be done with high level Normal Cats and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], as you can build a stack before you hit the base. Area Attackers like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] also help by clearing the way for Bahamut. Start by stacking a few [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] to quickly kill the Mesocosmocyclone and damage the Bore enough for Bahamut to kill it in a few hits. You can also use [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] to help deal with the Bore. It is also recommended to use [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Val Val Cat]] or [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Awesome]] using Cat Combos such as [[Legs for Days (Combo)|Legs for Days]] and [[Mo' Hawks (Combo)|Mo' Hawks]] together effectively for a longer, more tedious battle, but it isn't hard to come out on top.

